From afb6b070544d6fc5e8ff941232647860761cede7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anisetti Avinash Krishna <anisetti.avinash.krishna@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix periodic capture dropouts by making ALSA pipe writer
 non-blocking

StreamAlsaMonoPipe::start() created the input-side MonoPipe sink with
makeSink(mIsInput), which passed true (blocking) for input streams,
contradicting the method's own comment ("Do not block the writer
when it is on our thread").

The HAL's capture I/O thread continuously drains the real ALSA
hardware ring via proxy_read_with_retries() and pushes samples into
a software MonoPipe consumed by AudioFlinger's transfer() calls. With
a blocking sink, any brief delay in AudioFlinger draining the pipe
caused the capture thread's write() to block, which in turn stalled
it from re-draining the actual ALSA hardware ring. This allowed the
hardware ring to back up (observed up to ~854ms / 87% of polled
samples over the configured buffer size) and eventually overrun,
producing periodic ~70ms silence gaps roughly every 0.65s in
recordings.

Fix: always construct the input sink as non-blocking (makeSink(false))
so the capture thread never stalls on the downstream pipe, regardless
of how fast the consumer drains it.

Verified via live polling of /proc/asound/cardN/pcmNc/sub0/status
during capture (buffer overrun samples dropped from 87% to 0%, mean
backlog from ~412ms to ~14ms) and via audio analysis of recordings
from the built-in mic, a USB headset mic, and a Bluetooth SCO headset
mic, all showing zero periodic dropouts post-fix.

Note: on A17 this fix lands in StreamAlsaMonoPipe.cpp rather than
StreamAlsa.cpp, since StreamPrimary now inherits from a dedicated
StreamAlsaMonoPipe class (the base StreamAlsa class on A17 is a
simpler direct-passthrough implementation with no MonoPipe sink).

Test: Manual capture via built-in/USB/Bluetooth mic, verified no
      periodic silence gaps; confirmed /proc/asound avail/hw_ptr
      backlog eliminated.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1695
Signed-off-by: Anisetti Avinash Krishna <anisetti.avinash.krishna@intel.com>
---
 audio/aidl/default/alsa/StreamAlsaMonoPipe.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/alsa/StreamAlsaMonoPipe.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/alsa/StreamAlsaMonoPipe.cpp
index 3738f3056f..34bfb5f6dd 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/alsa/StreamAlsaMonoPipe.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/alsa/StreamAlsaMonoPipe.cpp
@@ -79,7 +79,9 @@ StreamAlsaMonoPipe::~StreamAlsaMonoPipe() {
         return status;
     }
     for (size_t i = 0; i < alsaDeviceProxies.size(); ++i) {
-        auto sink = makeSink(mIsInput);  // Do not block the writer when it is on our thread.
+        // Writer here is our own capture io thread; it must never block on the pipe,
+        // otherwise it stalls draining the ALSA hardware ring and causes capture overruns.
+        auto sink = makeSink(false);
         if (sink != nullptr) {
             sinks.push_back(sink);
         } else {
